{"content":"# Validation Report — collatz_tests\n\nPreliminary runs validating each experiment against its spec pre-registration.\nNumbers are from small exploratory runs (FAST128/GMP, DEBUG where noted); they\nestablish that the suite computes the right objects and reproduces the expected\nqualitative laws. They are **not** large-scale results.\n\n## H — congruence gate (the load-bearing identity)\nVerifies `x_n ≡ Σ_{k=1}^r 3^{k-1} 2^{-(b_{n-k}+…+b_{n-1})} (mod 3^r)`, which the\ncritique (`critiques/dc_1.md`) flagged as unverified before reliance.\n\n- FAST128, seeds 3–9999, r≤8, 6 sampled n each: **226 128 / 226 128 match**, 0 overflow.\n- GMP, seed 9 999 999 999 999 999, r=12, n up to 155 (values ≫ 2¹²⁸): **144 / 144 match**.\n\n**PASS.** The identity holds; downstream code may rely on it.\n\n## A — height-tail & critical census\nPre-registered: `log2 Pr(h≥H) ≈ −H + C`.\n\n- Octave 17, 65 536 seeds: per-step slopes of `log2(tail/seeds)` over H=2…12\n  average ≈ **−1.0** (range −0.88…−1.10). Mean height ≈ 1.17.\n\n**PASS** (slope −1 confirmed).\n\n## B — Cramér-tilt law on critical excursions\nPre-registered: critical-excursion bulk → `p^(1)_b = 3·4^{−b}`,\nentropy-per-digit → `H₂(3/4)=0.8113`.\n\n- Octave 24, `--crit-mode height`, boundary-excluded **middle** segments,\n  length 16–31 (38 402 segs): `p̂₁=0.686` (annealed 0.5, critical 0.75),\n  **KL→p^(1)=0.229 < KL→annealed=0.403**.\n- Full segments dilute toward annealed — launch/exit boundary layers, exactly\n  what the boundary-layer test isolates.\n\n**PASS in direction** (bulk leans to the Cramér tilt). Full convergence needs\nlarger octaves / longer excursions.\n\n## C — defect windows\nPre-registered: ordinary windows decay; no persistent residue resonance.\n\n- `|W|` at s=0 (residue Weyl sum) decays with window length\n  (0.31 @ L16 → 0.18 @ L64). Accelerated orbits terminate at 1, so single-orbit\n  windows are short — the asymptotic decay properly lives in E/F.\n\n## D — post-exit taboo\nPre-registered: post-exit windows separated from `p^(1)` and/or `M_post(1)<1`.\n\n- Octave 22, 7 675 windows: **KL→p=0.178 ≪ KL→p^(1)=0.566**, mean\n  `M_post(1)=0.991<1` (52 % subcritical). Post-exit relaxes toward annealed,\n  away from the critical tilt.\n\n**PASS** (taboo / entropy-space repulsion present).\n\n## E — exact residue-height operator gaps\nPre-registered: nontrivial sectors below trivial, `ρ(L_χ) ≤ (1−κ_Q)ρ(L_0)`.\n\n- Q=27, L=24, R=4, Bmax=20: every nontrivial mult-3^r sector strictly below\n  trivial. gap_ratio 0.86–0.93 (s=0), 0.89–0.99 (s=1). At s=1 the\n  lowest-frequency sector (k=1) has the smallest gap (0.994) — matches the\n  manuscript's \"a high ascent cannot also hold a residue resonance\".\n\n**PASS** (finite character-sector gaps present).\n\n## F — exact gap vs annealed Fourier\nPre-registered: compare exact `ρ` to `|p̂(ξ)| = 1/√(5−4cos 2πξ)`.\n\n- Q=27,81, Bmax=24: exact gap ratios deviate from the annealed value by\n  **±0.1…0.36**. `rho_annealed` and `rho_exact` are reported separately and\n  genuinely differ → the i.i.d. shadow is *not* the exact coupled gap; the\n  \"finiteness leak\" is real and κ_Q must be measured, not assumed.\n\n## G — trace / determinant shadows\n- `tr(L¹)=0`, `tr(L²)=1.5`; `det(1−zL)` smooth and positive\n  (0.95 @ z=0.25 → 0.82 @ z=0.5), no spurious peripheral structure at small (Q,L).\n\n## I — quenched spectral-shadow search (capstone)\n`shadow_flag` requires `max_{Q,χ,s}|W| ≥ δ` **and** `≥ 3×` a length-scaled null\n(`rms(weights)/√len`), to defeat short-window + max-over-grid inflation (the raw\nδ-only flag saturates at 100 %).\n\n- Octave 20, 20 000 seeds, moduli {9,27,81}: **4.8 %** of 222 498 windows flag.\n- By label: **critical_C_A 8.3 % > high_ascent 5.8 % > post_exit 3.7 %**\n  (critical likeliest to carry a shadow; post-exit least — taboo-consistent).\n- By length: shadow rate **grows** 0.3 % → 2.9 % → 7.9 % → **97.8 %** (len 64+,\n  n=44). Long excursions almost always exceed the null — the candidate\n  \"spectral shadow made visible\". Caveats: small long-window sample; the null\n  may weaken at large L. Follow-up: relate flagged windows to E/F operator gaps,\n  scale Q and sample size.\n\n## Open item\nThe \"C_A-critical\" definition is project-internal; `--crit-mode {height|vsq}`\nis provided and defaults to `height`. Confirm the formal certificate before\ntreating B/D/I critical labels as canonical.\n","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/c_suite/VALIDATION_REPORT.md","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false}